package kyber

// Fixed ML-KEM-768 / ML-KEM-1024 Known Answer Test vectors.
//
// Generated with Go 1.25.0 crypto/mlkem; seed = SHA256("kyber-go-kat:<name>:<i>:d") || SHA256("kyber-go-kat:<name>:<i>:z")
//
// These vectors were produced by running the Go standard library's
// crypto/mlkem package (an independent FIPS 203 implementation, distinct
// from this package's own code) with the fixed, reproducible seeds
// described above, and recording its outputs (encapsulation key,
// ciphertext, and shared secret). They are not official NIST ACVP known
// answer vectors, but they do provide a fixed-value cross-implementation
// check that this package agrees byte-for-byte with an independent FIPS
// 203 implementation, which a pure roundtrip test cannot provide. See
// TestKAT in kat_test.go for how these are checked. ML-KEM-512 is not
// implemented by crypto/mlkem, so it is covered separately by
// TestKAT512CrossImplementationHash in kat_test.go.
